WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.709
John: Good morning, Hank, it's Monday August
3rd, it's Esther Day.

00:00:02.709 --> 00:00:04.940
You'll never guess where I've found myself.

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.419
Hank, I'm in Agloe, New York.

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:11.110
So Hank Agloe is here or possibly here or
possibly here; it's hard to be certain when

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:15.320
you're talking about a place that is only
sometimes real, so anyway here's some footage

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:17.930
from what I think is Agloe for Esther Day.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:22.650
On Esther Day we remember our friend Esther
Earl as she wanted us to, by celebrating love

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.310
in all its many splendors.

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.930
Not just romantic love, but the love within
families and friendships.

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.090
Today is the day we say "I love you" to those
people even when it's hard, in fact especially

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:33.090
when it's hard.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.809
It's also the one day a year that Hank and
I acknowledge our love for each other verbally

00:00:36.809 --> 00:00:41.789
so OK, in accordance with Esther's wishes,
Hank, I reluctantly acknowledge that I love

00:00:41.789 --> 00:00:42.789
you immensely.

00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:46.630
Hank, when I've gone through challenging times
because of the bad wiring in my brain or physical

00:00:46.630 --> 00:00:50.969
illness or whatever, it gets very hard for
me to escape the prison of my own brain.

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:56.179
Like the pain/fear/obsessiveness becomes so
consuming that I struggle to empathize or

00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:57.179
listen well.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:00.179
And this can become a vicious cycle, like
you're in so much pain that you become so

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:03.870
self-involved that it becomes difficult to
connect to anyone which in turn increases

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:06.160
the pain and the self-involvement and etc.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.280
I can't tell you how many times your patience
and empathy have shut down that spiral for

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.280
me.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.010
It's something you've done consistently for
me since you were like three.

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:18.870
So yeah, thank you and I just admire you a
lot and I think you're awesome and I love

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.870
you.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.660
If you don't know about Esther, check out
her book, you can also go to dftba.com or

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:27.520
tswgo.org to support the charity This Star
Won't Go Out which was created by Esther's

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.530
family and provides direct support to families
of children with cancer; links in the dooblydoo.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:35.030
Oh, also, I'm gonna do a question Tuesday
tomorrow Nerdfighters, so please leave me

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:37.680
questions, ideally brief ones, in comments.

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:39.720
Thank you, DFTBA.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.200
Hank, you'll see me tomorrow.

